; A named-let loop procedure is an ordinary value, on every substrate.
;
; R7RS 4.2.4 defines `(let loop ((v init) ...) body)` as a letrec binding, so
; `loop` may be stored, returned or passed on, and the procedure that escapes
; keeps the bindings its body closed over. Both escape shapes below must give the
; same answer under native `-r`, native AOT, `vm-src` and `vm-eskb`.
;
; THIS ENTRY EXISTS BECAUSE THEY USED TO DISAGREE, ON BOTH SIDES.
;
; NATIVE crashed. A named-let loop function's signature carries one capture
; POINTER per captured free variable — the per-call capture design that keeps
; concurrent invocations race-free — and is deliberately not the closure ABI, so
; a first-class reference fell through to the generic function-table path and
; yielded the bare function pointer. Calling the leaked procedure entered the
; loop function with its capture parameters filled from whatever the closure
; dispatcher happened to pass, and the first read of a captured variable
; dereferenced that as a capture cell:
;
;     native -r    "2|" then fatal SIGSEGV
;     native AOT   "2|" then fatal SIGSEGV, same fault address
;     vm-src       2|2|ALIVE                                (the VM was right)
;
; A first-class reference now materialises a real closure whose environment
; holds the address of each shared capture cell, with a per-loop trampoline
; forwarding those cells as the pointer arguments the loop function expects. The
; cells are arena storage, so the leaked procedure keeps reading and writing what
; the loop wrote through and it outlives the enclosing frame.
;
; THE VM had its own half, on the other axis: the compiled-bytecode route lost a
; loop procedure stored in a GLOBAL that the source route kept, and neither VM
; route could call one held in a LET-BOUND cell — both `ERROR: calling
; non-function ... argc=1 type=3`. Both are closed, so the contract is gated on
; all four axes here rather than filed.
;
; Native-only depth (six escape shapes, 15 checks) lives in
; tests/features/namedlet_escaped_closure_test.esk; this entry pins the two
; shapes the VM can express, so a regression on either substrate reds the gate.

; ---- escape through a global cell ----
(define g #f)
(define (f)
  (let ((acc 0))
    (let loop ((i 0))
      (if (< i 2) (begin (set! g loop) (set! acc (+ acc 1)) (loop (+ i 1))) acc))))
(display (f))
(display "|")
(display (g 5))
(display "|ALIVE")
(newline)

; ---- escape through a let-bound cell ----
(define (probe)
  (let ((esc #f) (acc 0))
    (let loop ((i 0))
      (if (< i 2) (begin (set! esc loop) (set! acc (+ acc 1)) (loop (+ i 1))) acc))
    (esc 5)))
(display (probe))
(newline)
